# TUI-DESIGN-5 §3 / §10 (slot R5-3): `/context` then `/compact` under `--mock` at 120x40, plus the
# `nothing to compact` branch and the `compaction is off` branch. Hermetic: `--mock` only, no network, no key.
#
# MODE — the SHIPPED DEFAULT, deliberately. The scenario takes no `--mode`: R13 put `llm-jev` inside
#   `contextEnabled`, so the `ctx` status cell and the `/context` block are what an ORDINARY user sees. Pinning
#   this to `--mode jev-on` proved the feature in a mode nobody runs by default. The jev-only twin — where there
#   is no generator context and the cell must be ABSENT rather than `ctx —%` (§7 row 35) — is the second case in
#   `test/pty/round5.pty.test.ts`.
#
# run-smoke.sh rows for this scenario:
#   env    : r5-context) extra_env="$extra_env JEVCODE_CONTEXT_COMPACTION=code";;
#   check  : the block, the `ctx NN%` cell, and no `ctx —%` placeholder
#   select : sel_named r5-context && run r5-context 0 40 120 chat --mock
#
# What it proves, beyond "it renders":
#   - §3.2's three reads join into ONE block whose head is S48 and whose first row is `formatBudget`'s own text;
#   - §3.7's rungs: the per-file table with its reason column at 120 and 80, the count row alone at 40;
#   - §3.3: `/compact` after the run answers `availabilityError`'s generated live-only sentence (see step 6);
#   - §3.4: the engine's own `compaction:` notice is unchanged and the `─ compaction ─` rule sits ABOVE it;
#   - G-R5-9: `assertNoKeyBytes` over every frame (the block prints paths and byte counts, never a key).

expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.4

# 1 — `/context` before any run: §7 row 36's own sentence, not an empty block
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect no run is live
sleep 0.3
mark context-no-run

# 2 — a run, so `status().context` exists; `--mock` steps are deterministic
send do a thing
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 1.2
mark run-live

# 3 — the full block at 120x40: the head, `budget`, `recent steps`, `files in view` and the per-file table
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect context [·-] step
sleep 0.4
mark context-120

# 4 — the 40-column rung: the same head, the count row, and NO per-file rows (§3.7)
resize 40 40
sleep 0.8
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 0.4
mark context-40

# 5 — the 80-column rung: the per-file rows are back and the reason column survives (§3.7, §14.2 finding 1)
resize 40 80
sleep 0.8
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 0.4
mark context-80

# 6 — `/compact` AFTER the mock run has ended. The step this replaced waited for S57 (`nothing to compact`),
#     which only a LIVE run can answer; by the time the four `/context` reads above have been typed the
#     `--mock` run is long finished, so the scenario timed out for 67 s on every invocation and then failed on
#     the exit code rather than on anything about `/compact`. `availabilityError`'s own live-only sentence is
#     what this position actually proves — and that it is the GENERATED one, never a hand-written twin.
#     S57 / S58a (`nothing to compact` vs `compaction is off`) are covered live in
#     `test/unit/cli/session*.test.ts`; a pty scenario cannot type into a live `--mock` run without the
#     stdin-starvation hazard of docs/research/tui/20-pty-driver-findings.md §5.
resize 40 120
sleep 0.6
send /compact
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect needs a live run
sleep 0.3
mark compact-after-run

send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
